# ShowCrafter UI Rules

Before UI work, read the local design-system skill:

- `.agents/skills/showcrafter-design-system/SKILL.md`
- `.claude/skills/showcrafter-design-system/SKILL.md`

## Product Feel

ShowCrafter should feel like a precise creative tool for planning real
pyromusical shows. Keep app and admin screens dense, calm, scannable, and
work-focused. Avoid cheap neon, crypto dashboards, oversized marketing cards in
tool surfaces, and ember/burnt-orange palettes.

## Components

- Prefer `platform/app/components/ui` primitives for product UI.
- Generated Radix/shadcn primitives live in `platform/components/ui`; use them
  when extending the generated layer.
- Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils`.
- Use `platform/app/globals.css` tokens.
- `platform/app/components/ui/styles.ts` is a legacy shared-class bridge. Prefer
  variants on primitives over adding more route-level class strings there.
- Use lucide icons for icon buttons when available.
- Keep controls stable in size so hover, selected, loading, and dynamic text
  states do not shift layout.

## Loading

Keep stable chrome visible while data loads: titles, descriptions, labels,
table headers, form section headings, tabs, and navigation. Skeletonise only
data-driven fields, active values, badges, preview media, and controls whose
value is still loading. Match loaded dimensions closely.

## App And Admin Patterns

- `AppShell` owns the authenticated customer shell.
- `AdminShell` owns admin chrome.
- `/catalogue`, `/library`, and `/library/[id]` are guest browse routes. Use
  marketing chrome for guests and `AppShell` for authenticated visitors.
- Filter every admin navigation item by the permission required by its route.
  Keep route and server-action authorisation as the security boundary.
- Give mobile users a visible sidebar trigger outside the closed sheet. Render
  one main landmark per page shell.
- Firework, effect, and style-default editors share `FireworkEditorShell`,
  compact preview transport controls, history/JSON panels, and scoped
  `FireworkRenderControls`.
- Style-default pages should keep a narrower side rail than the full
  firework/effect editors.
- Heavy WebGL, shader, and editor components should not be imported globally.

## Product Truthfulness

- Keep upload analysis quiet. The final Generate control is the explicit action
  that creates the show and starts cue generation.
- In `fast` mode, identify the fast planner and hide LLM model selection. Expose
  model choice and model cost only in `llm` mode. The server must revalidate the
  current mode on submit.
- Explore content comes from database-managed `show_presets`. New, imported,
  and duplicated presets are drafts until an admin publishes them.
- Show persisted like state and aggregate counts. Never invent likes, views,
  popularity, or social proof from IDs, sort order, or seeded constants.
- Use factual shelf names and build See all from the complete matching query,
  not a deduplicated landing-shelf partition. Query failures belong in a safe
  retry boundary rather than an empty-state message.
- Reset and delete controls must describe and invoke the real backend action.
  Confirm destructive Auth deletion and never toast success for a no-op.

## Editor Correctness

- Include every simulation input and launch-position coordinate in replay cache
  keys. A visually relevant edit must invalidate the preview.
- Snapshot the editor signature when a save starts. Apply the returned snapshot
  only if local state still matches it, preserving newer edits. Update the
  latest-signature ref in a layout effect, not a passive effect or render.
- Treat version-history recording as best-effort. A history write failure must
  not turn a successful primary save into a failure.
- Centralise physical ranges, clamp invalid negative speed and life values, and
  keep controls, validation, actions, defaults, and renderer bounds aligned.
- Put accessible names on slider thumbs and other interactive primitives, not
  only on non-interactive wrappers. Put the label target ID on the focusable
  thumb. Do not expose a Preview action unless it performs a real preview.

## Shader Covers

Shows and presets store serialisable `cover_shader` JSON. Use
`platform/lib/shader-cover.ts` helpers for generation, parsing, normalisation,
and deterministic seeded covers. Do not hand-roll incompatible cover objects in
routes.
